{
  "quest.07105D263E94F5A2.title": "What to Do in the Nether?",
  "quest.07105D263E94F5A2.quest_subtitle": "Safe activities receive separate paths instead of one long journey",
  "quest.07105D263E94F5A2.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: understand the new Nether chapter and choose only activities for which you are prepared.",
    "",
    "Preparing for the Nether ends after your first marked route and safe return. This separate chapter now collects optional activities and later progression paths inside the Nether.",
    "",
    "The first two branches teach one safe Piglin barter and a short resource trip for Netherrack and Nether Quartz. Both are optional and block no later path.",
    "",
    "The third branch explains the Nether Fortress. It is important for Blaze Rods and Nether Wart but contains Blazes and Wither Skeletons. Start this path only with the required equipment and a secured retreat.",
    "",
    "Bastion Remnants will also receive a separate advanced branch. They contain Piglin Brutes, guarded containers, and many falling hazards; a Golden Helmet alone does not make a Bastion safe.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you understand the chapter structure. You do not need to leave the Overworld for this step.",
  ],
  "task.18216E374FA506B3.title": "I know the planned Nether paths",

  "quest.1C83F0A24D6E917B.title": "Plan a Small Resource Trip",
  "quest.1C83F0A24D6E917B.quest_subtitle": "Only as far as the next safe mining place and back",
  "quest.1C83F0A24D6E917B.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: choose a safe nearby mining place along your marked route.",
    "",
    "Bring at least an Iron Pickaxe or a better Pickaxe, your Golden Helmet, a Shield, Flint and Steel, eight substantial cooked foods, 16 Torches, and 32 Cobblestone. Store unnecessary valuables at home.",
    "",
    "Stay within your already marked route for this trip. A suitable place has firm ground, a clear retreat, and nearby Cobblestone cover. Do not mine above Lava, beneath an open ceiling, or beside a drop.",
    "",
    "Netherrack and Nether Quartz Ore occur in every Nether biome. You therefore do not need to find a particular biome or extend your safe route.",
    "",
    "Ignore Gold Ore, Glowstone on high ceilings, and unfamiliar structures for now. Those targets need additional rules. Retreat immediately if a Ghast, Piglin Brute, fire, or Lava threatens the way home.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark at the safe mining place only after checking equipment, footing, cover, and retreat.",
  ],
  "task.2D94A1B35E7FA28C.title": "I checked a safe nearby mining place",

  "quest.3EA5B2C46F80939D.title": "Collect Some Netherrack",
  "quest.3EA5B2C46F80939D.quest_subtitle": "The Nether's soft red ground stone",
  "quest.3EA5B2C46F80939D.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: collect 16 Netherrack at the checked mining place.",
    "",
    "Netherrack is the common reddish stone of the Nether. A Pickaxe breaks it very quickly. Hold the mouse button only briefly so that you do not accidentally dig too far.",
    "",
    "Mine individual visible blocks while standing on firm ground. Never dig straight down or blindly upward: Lava, a cavity, or a free fall may hide behind the thin rock.",
    "",
    "Fire on Netherrack burns indefinitely until extinguished. Put out one reachable flame as learned with a left click without stepping into it. Retreat if the fire spreads or is difficult to reach.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes as soon as 16 Netherrack are in your inventory at once. Keep some Cobblestone as clearly recognisable protection and marker blocks; Netherrack does not replace it on this route.",
  ],
  "task.4FB6C3D57091A4AE.title": "Hold 16 Netherrack in the inventory at once",

  "quest.50C7D4E681A2B5BF.title": "Find Your First Nether Quartz",
  "quest.50C7D4E681A2B5BF.quest_subtitle": "White inclusions inside Netherrack",
  "quest.50C7D4E681A2B5BF.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: collect four Nether Quartz.",
    "",
    "Nether Quartz Ore has bright white inclusions inside Netherrack. It occurs in every Nether biome, although it may still be absent by chance along your short route. Search only safe walls that you can reach from the ground.",
    "",
    "Mine the ore with a Pickaxe without Silk Touch. It drops Nether Quartz and gives some experience. A Silk Touch Pickaxe drops the Ore block instead and does not complete this task; use another Pickaxe in that case.",
    "",
    "Never enlarge a dangerous cavity merely to reach another Ore. Four Quartz are enough. If none lies along the safe route, you may continue this optional quest later.",
    "",
    "Nether Quartz is used later for bright building blocks and various Redstone components. Four Quartz can become one Block of Quartz, but that block cannot be turned back into four Quartz.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes as soon as four Nether Quartz are in your inventory at once.",
  ],
  "task.61D8E5F792B3C6C0.title": "Hold 4 Nether Quartz in the inventory at once",

  "quest.72E9F608A3C4D7D1.title": "Bring the Samples Home Safely",
  "quest.72E9F608A3C4D7D1.quest_subtitle": "A resource trip ends beyond the original portal",
  "quest.72E9F608A3C4D7D1.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: return to the Overworld through your original portal with Netherrack and Nether Quartz.",
    "",
    "End the trip while the known route is still safe. Follow the Torch sides of your Cobblestone markers to the portal shelter, close the protected entrance behind you, and briefly check that nothing followed you before using the portal.",
    "",
    "Return through the same portal and store both samples at home. Do not postpone the retreat for one more Ore block or additional experience.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark in the Overworld only after Netherrack and Nether Quartz are stored safely and you know that the marked route remains usable.",
    "",
    "Reward: Eight Cobblestone replace some possible protection blocks; five experience points recognise the safe return.",
  ],
  "task.03FA0719B4D5E8E2.title": "I returned safely to the Overworld with both samples",

  "quest.78FAD3D980F349BA.title": "Equip Yourself for the Nether Fortress",
  "quest.78FAD3D980F349BA.quest_subtitle": "A long search and confined fights need larger reserves",
  "quest.78FAD3D980F349BA.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold the minimum equipment for searching for a Nether Fortress at the same time.",
    "",
    "Bring a Sword and Pickaxe made from at least Iron or a better material, a Shield, 64 Cobblestone, and 16 substantial cooked foods. The automatic tasks check these items without consuming them.",
    "",
    "Wear the Golden Helmet for ordinary Piglins. Your Chestplate, Leggings, and Boots should each be made from at least Iron or a better material. Repair or replace heavily damaged equipment before leaving.",
    "",
    "Also bring Flint and Steel, at least 32 Torches, and additional Cobblestone markers. A Bow with at least 32 Arrows is strongly recommended but not required. A Milk Bucket can remove the Wither effect, but it also removes every other status effect.",
    "",
    "Sleep in the safe Bed one last time, record the portal and shelter coordinates, and start with full Health and a full Hunger bar. Remove unnecessary valuables from the inventory.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only while wearing the Golden Helmet plus at least an Iron Chestplate, Iron Leggings, and Iron Boots or better pieces, and after completing the additional checklist.",
  ],
  "task.36AD35CCA4724357.title": "Hold 1 Iron-or-better Sword",
  "task.1B63A993ED3C4DB3.title": "Hold 1 Iron-or-better Pickaxe",
  "task.3E4AF2D781EC4B57.title": "Hold 1 Shield",
  "task.65C89337665C4E28.title": "Hold 64 Cobblestone",
  "task.21D6CE3AD23A412B.title": "Hold 16 substantial cooked foods",
  "task.5583FD1F127A4B12.title": "Golden Helmet and at least Iron Armour worn; reserve checked",

  "quest.73B2B39D1C674728.title": "Find a Nether Fortress",
  "quest.73B2B39D1C674728.quest_subtitle": "Dark-red bridges and pillars instead of black Bastion walls",
  "quest.73B2B39D1C674728.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: find a Nether Fortress without losing the safe route home.",
    "",
    "Nether Fortresses are made from dark-red Nether Bricks. From a distance, you can often recognise long straight bridges, massive pillars, and open corridors. A Bastion Remnant is instead built mainly from black Blackstone and is not your target.",
    "",
    "The image shows a typical Fortress segment with long Nether Brick bridges, a junction, and massive supporting pillars.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/nether_fortress.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Begin at the protected portal shelter and extend your known marker rule carefully. Record coordinates at important turns. The Torch side of every upper Cobblestone block continues to point home.",
    "",
    "Do not search across an open Lava sea or build a long unprotected bridge. If you must tunnel blindly, remain behind Cobblestone, listen for Lava, and open only a small area at a time. Return regularly before food, blocks, or durability runs low.",
    "",
    "A Fortress may be far away. You may divide the search across several journeys. Do not enter a Bastion or force a dangerous route merely to complete this optional quest quickly.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after safely reaching the Fortress's Nether Bricks, recording its coordinates, and checking a completely marked route back to the portal shelter. Do not go deep inside yet.",
  ],
  "task.22D566F202A7429E.title": "I found a Nether Fortress with a safe retreat",

  "quest.3D912A104D4A4E4E.title": "Secure the Fortress Entrance",
  "quest.3D912A104D4A4E4E.quest_subtitle": "Build a retreat room before exploring the first corridor",
  "quest.3D912A104D4A4E4E.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: build a small protected retreat room at the reached edge of the Fortress.",
    "",
    "Choose an entrance with firm ground and a direct connection to your marked route home. Build a closed Cobblestone retreat room with a roof, a lit interior, and a clearly marked outside.",
    "",
    "Leave only two blocks of open height in the passage toward the Fortress. You can pass through, but a taller Wither Skeleton cannot. This barrier stops neither Blaze fire nor smaller enemies; remain alert and close openings with full blocks when danger appears.",
    "",
    "Record the retreat room's coordinates. From the room, first check the route to the portal and then only the immediately adjoining Fortress corridor. Torches act as route markers here but do not make the Fortress completely safe from enemy spawning.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark inside the closed room after checking its roof, floor, marked route home, two-block passage, and quickly accessible Cobblestone blocks.",
  ],
  "task.0F3B0653610D483B.title": "I have a protected and marked Fortress entrance",

  "quest.676BFD158DEB4F7F.title": "Recognise the Fortress Hazards",
  "quest.676BFD158DEB4F7F.quest_subtitle": "Blazes, Wither Skeletons, and narrow bridges need different reactions",
  "quest.676BFD158DEB4F7F.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: know the most important hazards before fighting inside the Fortress.",
    "",
    "Blazes are floating yellow enemies. They briefly catch fire before firing several fireballs. A full Cobblestone wall reliably breaks their line of sight; a Shield and Bow help but do not replace that cover.",
    "",
    "Wither Skeletons are tall dark Skeletons carrying Stone Swords. Their hit causes Wither: your Hearts darken and you continue losing Health for a while. Never fight at the edge of a bridge. Retreat through your passage with only two blocks of open height, which they cannot pass.",
    "",
    "Ordinary Skeletons, Magma Cubes, and other enemies may also appear inside or near the Fortress. Do not open a Chest yet and do not chase an enemy around a corner. An unknown corridor may contain more enemies or a sheer drop.",
    "",
    "From left to right, the image shows a Blaze, a Wither Skeleton, and a Magma Cube.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/fortress_hazards.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "If several hazards meet, block the opening and return home. Food does not heal immediately: it first restores Hunger so that natural regeneration can begin when the bar is sufficiently full.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark inside the retreat room when you can name a safe retreat reaction for a Blaze, a Wither Skeleton, and an overcrowded corridor.",
  ],
  "task.54A8AA81D49E4187.title": "I know solid cover, the two-block barrier, and full retreat",

  "quest.5B0F14AD63E74BD3.title": "Obtain Two Blaze Rods",
  "quest.5B0F14AD63E74BD3.quest_subtitle": "Fight only one Blaze at a time from solid cover",
  "quest.5B0F14AD63E74BD3.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: defeat Blazes in a controlled way until two Blaze Rods are in your inventory at once.",
    "",
    "First prepare a clear retreat behind a Cobblestone corner. Do not fight on an open bridge. When one Blaze appears, move fully behind the wall during its burning attack phase and wait out the fireballs there.",
    "",
    "If you cannot reach the full wall in time, raise the Shield with a right click and look directly at the Blaze. The raised Shield can block its fireballs from the front. It does not protect against shots from the side or behind, so solid cover remains safer.",
    "",
    "After the volley, attack with a Bow from cover or approach only on safe ground for individual fully charged Sword strikes. Do not start a melee fight while several Blazes are visible or another enemy can appear behind you.",
    "",
    "If you are burning, immediately enter cover, watch your Hearts, and eat when Hunger is missing. Fire Resistance from a later potion or a random Piglin barter helps against fire but does not protect against every attack and is not required.",
    "",
    "A block surrounded by a small cage with a spinning Blaze inside is a Blaze Spawner. Do not stand beside it without protection and do not destroy it yet; secure only an approach and retreat as soon as several Blazes appear.",
    "",
    "The image shows the Spawner on a typical raised Nether Brick section of the Fortress.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/blaze_spawner.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Blazes do not drop a Rod after every fight. End the trip and try again later rather than continuing with damaged equipment. The automatic task completes with two Blaze Rods.",
  ],
  "task.31EF76AC88474111.title": "Hold 2 Blaze Rods in the inventory at once",

  "quest.15F17869891E4CE0.title": "Secure Nether Wart and Soul Sand",
  "quest.15F17869891E4CE0.quest_subtitle": "The foundation of later potions also grows at home",
  "quest.15F17869891E4CE0.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: collect at least four Nether Wart and four Soul Sand.",
    "",
    "Nether Wart grows in some Nether Fortresses as small red beds at the foot of certain staircases. Not every Fortress contains such a garden. If yours has none, search for another Fortress on a later prepared journey; do not enter a Bastion for this task.",
    "",
    "Secure both ends of the corridor first and check the floor and ceiling. Mature Nether Wart is large and dark red and drops several Wart; small growth stages drop only one. Break it with a left click and collect four blocks of the Soul Sand beneath it too.",
    "",
    "Nether Wart grows on Soul Sand in every dimension. It needs neither Water nor Farmland, and light does not affect its growth speed. You can therefore create a small protected potion-ingredient farm beside your home later.",
    "",
    "The two automatic tasks complete as soon as four Nether Wart and four Soul Sand are in your inventory at once. Retreat afterward; more Fortress rooms are not your goal yet.",
  ],
  "task.0966E3DA03134381.title": "Hold 4 Nether Wart in the inventory at once",
  "task.25DF04566B784491.title": "Hold 4 Soul Sand in the inventory at once",

  "quest.734140DAA3E544D2.title": "Return from the Fortress",
  "quest.734140DAA3E544D2.quest_subtitle": "Blaze Rods and Nether Wart count only after a safe return",
  "quest.734140DAA3E544D2.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: bring your Blaze Rods, Nether Wart, and Soul Sand home through the original portal.",
    "",
    "Leave the Fortress through the secured entrance and follow only your marked route. Repair damaged route sections only from cover. If the route is blocked, retreat to the Fortress room instead of opening an unmarked shortcut.",
    "",
    "Store both Blaze Rods at home; one will later be needed for a Brewing Stand, while the other can become Blaze Powder. Do not process them until the brewing guide explains both steps.",
    "",
    "Place the four Soul Sand beside one another in a protected place and plant one Nether Wart on each with a right click. Wait until the plants are large and dark red before harvesting. Water is unnecessary.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark in the Overworld only after the Rods are stored safely, the small Nether Wart farm is planted, and you can find the Fortress route again later.",
    "",
    "Reward: 16 Cobblestone replace some protection and route blocks; ten experience points recognise the safe Fortress return.",
  ],
  "task.4C2E1220EA4C4B18.title": "I returned safely and planted the Nether Wart farm",
}
